  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9b3638b8-f15d-4293-968d-d093eb592d2c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 194px;\"/></p><p>By Brewster’s law at complete polarization, refracted ray and reflected ray are perpendicular to each other.</p><p>As angle of reflection will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. Therefore, angle of refraction will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math>.</p>",
